WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.201 --> 00:00:02.470
(dramatic music)

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:04.760
- [Narrator] Hong Kong-based
entrepreneur, Ben Cheng,

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:06.000
is packing up.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.650
- The plan is some designers,

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:10.980
developer, relocate later this year.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:12.100
- [Narrator] His company, Oursky,

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.020
has created apps for major finance

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:16.430
and fashion companies around the world.

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:17.620
- This is a product we developed.

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:20.520
It is a stylus for iPad.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.580
- [Narrator] Like the vast majority

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.240
of companies in Hong Kong,

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:25.450
Cheng says the city's quality of life,

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:26.800
widespread use of English

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:28.780
and business-friendly regulations

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:31.720
have created the ideal
place to build his business.

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:32.710
In the past decade,

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:34.940
Oursky has grown from
just three developers

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:37.133
to more than 60 employees.

00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:39.040
- This is one of our client's product.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:40.270
It is tracking my face

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:41.103
and if I move,

00:00:42.227 --> 00:00:44.530
the camera move with me.

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:45.640
- [Narrator] But now he says a sweeping

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:46.740
National Security Law

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:49.780
that was passed after a year
of pro-democracy protests

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:51.820
is threatening his business.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:54.490
It broadly criminalizes
secession, subversion,

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:56.990
terrorism, and collusion
with foreign governments

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:58.810
with up to life in prison.

00:00:58.810 --> 00:01:00.530
And the new law is pushing companies

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:03.283
like Cheng's to reconsider
their future in the city.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:06.000
- Singapore, Taipei and Tokyo,

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.403
we do consider like different cities.

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:11.750
- [Narrator] In August, a
poll by the American Chamber

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:13.280
of Commerce in Hong Kong found

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:15.820
that 39% of its members
who were surveyed said

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:17.350
they have plans to move capital,

00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:19.500
assets or operations out of the city

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.423
because of the National Security Law.

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:24.330
Several countries in the region

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:27.390
are making moves to sway
businesses in Hong Kong.

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:29.170
So what can these places offer companies

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:31.690
like Cheng's and which will he choose?

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:32.630
- What you need to do

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:33.963
from a site selection perspective

00:01:33.963 --> 00:01:36.120
is you need to look at, first of all,

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:40.065
what are those factors
both critical and important

00:01:40.065 --> 00:01:42.670
that drive the success of a business?

00:01:42.670 --> 00:01:44.570
- [Narrator] For nearly
30 years, John Evans

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:46.260
and his firm Tractus Asia,

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:48.360
have been advising
companies like Kellogg's,

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:49.460
Boeing and MetLife

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:52.386
where to set up offices in the region.

00:01:52.386 --> 00:01:55.110
He says the most
important factor companies

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:56.990
have historically looked at first

00:01:56.990 --> 00:01:59.150
is the cost of operating in a city,

00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:02.240
which includes real estate,
salaries and utilities.

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:04.670
Companies have gravitated to Hong Kong

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:06.900
or Singapore because of corporate taxes,

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:09.493
which are far lower than
Australia and Japan.

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:14.640
Next up, the city's
connectivity to other places.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:16.300
This is everything from how easy it is

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:17.280
to get to the airport

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:19.300
to how long you have to sit on a plane

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:21.230
until you meet your client.

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:22.210
Before the pandemic,

00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:23.870
airports in Seoul and Hong Kong

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:26.010
have the most number of destinations,

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:28.963
with Singapore, Tokyo and
Taipei not far behind.

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:32.870
Companies need to be able to rely

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:35.560
on an independent and
efficient legal system

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:37.090
so if they ever go to court,

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:40.090
they can be assured that
they'll be given a fair trial.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.330
South Korea and Japan

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:43.450
are often held up as Asian democracies

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:45.043
with effective judiciaries.

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:50.650
And finally, an increasingly
important factor is risk.

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:52.930
- The Fukushima nuclear disaster,

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:54.680
that's when C suites started

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:56.770
to think about risk more important.

00:02:56.770 --> 00:02:58.951
Then with the rising costs of China

00:02:58.951 --> 00:03:01.125
and the US-China trade war,

00:03:01.125 --> 00:03:03.940
followed very closely by COVID,

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:06.913
risk has really become I
think that important factor.

00:03:06.913 --> 00:03:09.530
- [Narrator] Evans says Hong
Kong's National Security Law

00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:11.770
chips away at the city's rule of law

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:14.713
and increases the political
risk companies can face.

00:03:15.716 --> 00:03:20.330
And that's a cost Ben Cheng
says his company can't afford.

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:21.820
- We start getting some letter

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:24.340
from the legal department of our clients,

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:26.710
asking about like where our data stored.

00:03:26.710 --> 00:03:29.380
The recent National
Security Law make them wary

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:32.690
about if they should
continue using our service.

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:33.640
- [Narrator] For some clients,

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:34.850
Cheng has had to comply

00:03:34.850 --> 00:03:37.280
with strict European Union data protection

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.070
and privacy regulations

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:40.800
but now he says he could be held liable

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:43.040
for violating those if Hong Kong police

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:44.420
use the National Security Law

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:46.840
during an investigation to collect data

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:48.920
or order it deleted online.

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:52.570
- This law will not undermine
human rights and freedoms.

00:03:52.570 --> 00:03:53.500
- [Narrator] But Hong Kong government

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:55.971
has said the law won't affect
people's basic freedoms

00:03:55.971 --> 00:03:58.140
and that only time and facts will tell

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:00.563
that the law will not
undermine human rights.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:04.140
But Cheng says this promise
doesn't reassure him.

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:06.610
And realizes he can't
store his clients' data

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:08.580
in Hong Kong and guarantee them

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:10.140
that it will be safe.

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:12.320
So he's chosen to move
part of his staff out

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:13.420
of the city.

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:15.940
His decision is based on two factors.

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:17.420
Being in a democratic country

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:19.080
where he can guarantee the protection

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:20.193
of his clients' data

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:22.390
and a city with a good quality of life

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:24.581
so he can attract talent.

00:04:24.581 --> 00:04:25.414
- So in the next phase,

00:04:25.414 --> 00:04:30.414
we are going to do is to set
up a new office in UK, London,

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:34.230
especially for storing data
for our Western clients.

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:36.840
And also, we will have
office in both Taipei

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:37.960
and in Japan.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:39.830
These two location are just very popular.

00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:41.270
So to retain our talent,

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:43.053
we have to open office there.

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:45.640
- [Narrator] There is one wildcard

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:48.280
that Cheng and other
companies could consider.

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:49.810
In a bid to lure businesses,

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:53.200
countries in the region are
planning special incentives.

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:54.530
Japan is discussing plans

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:57.740
to make it easier for people
in finance to get visas.

00:04:57.740 --> 00:05:00.080
Taiwan opened a dedicated
government office

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:01.830
to help companies move.

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:03.830
And one Australian lawmaker is pushing

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:05.856
to lower the corporate tax rate.

00:05:05.856 --> 00:05:09.060
- Your location decision
should never be driven

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:12.980
by incentives, be they
tax or non-tax incentives.

00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:15.500
Incentives are the icing on the cake.

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:18.646
It's the sweetener that
allows you to make a decision.

00:05:18.646 --> 00:05:21.550
- [Narrator] So which cities
have John Evans' clients

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:23.470
inquired about the most recently?

00:05:23.470 --> 00:05:25.470
- If China is the market you're pursuing,

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:27.590
you might as well set up
in a place like Shanghai.

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:30.090
If you're concerned about risks

00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:32.810
that come with doing business in China,

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:36.470
then Singapore by far is the easiest

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:40.490
and most effective location
to quickly relocate out

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:41.323
of Hong Kong.

00:05:42.310 --> 00:05:43.530
- [Narrator] For now, only a handful

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:45.130
of companies have publicly announced

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:46.960
their Hong Kong departure.

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:48.440
The New York Times said it would move part

00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:49.410
of its staff to Seoul

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:52.350
because the National Security
Law has created uncertainty

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:54.450
about the newspaper's operations.

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:56.360
And noted difficulties obtaining visas

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:58.630
for some Hong Kong-based staffers.

00:05:58.630 --> 00:06:00.610
While South Korean tech company, Naver,

00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:03.610
announced it had moved its
data backup center to Singapore

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:06.880
according to a statement
provided to local media.

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:09.110
Ben Cheng says it's just a matter of time

00:06:09.110 --> 00:06:12.870
before other businesses follow
their lead out of Hong Kong.

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:16.210
- We used to have an
advantage here in Hong Kong.

00:06:16.210 --> 00:06:18.740
We are in the middle of East and West.

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:21.160
So a lot of companies
setting up office here

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:25.260
would enjoy both the culture
of the Western market.

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:28.230
At the same time, they
can also go into China

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:32.080
but now, people realize that
they have to rethink Hong Kong

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:33.285
in the future.

00:06:33.285 --> 00:06:36.035
(dramatic music)

